body:
`autoLayoutResult` is set to `null` when `schema.customFields?.length` is truthy, which prevents `effectiveModalSize` from auto-upgrading for flat forms that use `customFields`. Since the flat-field renderer still applies `applyAutoLayout(...)` for `customFields`, the modal size upgrade should also consider that case (likely only gate on `sections`, not `customFields`).
```suggestion
    if (schema.sections?.length) return null;
    return applyAutoLayout(formFields, objectSchema, schema.columns, schema.mode);
  }, [formFields, objectSchema, schema.columns, schema.mode, schema.sections]);
```
